# US-Blo Optimized Parameter List v2 (2025-10-30)
# Site: US-Blo (Temperate Deciduous Broadleaf Forest)
# PFT 1: Needleleaf Evergreen Temperate Tree
#
# Based on surrogate robustness diagnostics that revealed:
# 1. Poor surrogate quality (R² < 0.70) due to weak parameter influences
# 2. Insufficient dynamic range (GPP range only 106 gC/m²/year)
# 3. Parameter identifiability issues (perfect correlations)
#
# KEY CHANGES FROM ORIGINAL:
# 1. Added photosynthesis parameters (leafcn, flnr, slatop) -> strong GPP control
# 2. Removed redundant root pool parameters (kept only "t" pools, removed "a" and "m")
# 3. Kept most influential root parameters from sensitivity analysis
# 4. Adjusted ranges for temperate forest (not eucalyptus like AU-Tum)
#
# Format: parameter_name pft min max
# For ensemble: uniform sampling between min/max
# For MCMC: can optionally specify distributions in separate config

# ============================================================================
# PHOTOSYNTHESIS PARAMETERS (CRITICAL FOR GPP)
# ============================================================================

# Specific Leaf Area - top of canopy (m² leaf area / gC)
# Temperate deciduous: 0.015-0.030 m²/gC (thinner leaves than evergreen)
# Higher SLA = more leaf area = more light interception = higher GPP
# Expected impact: ±30-40% GPP change
slatop 1 0.015 0.030

# Leaf C:N ratio (gC/gN)
# Temperate deciduous: 20-40 (lower C:N than evergreen conifers)
# Lower C:N = more leaf N = higher vcmax25 = more photosynthesis
# ELM calculates: vcmax25 = f(1/leafcn, flnr)
# Expected impact: ±30-40% GPP change
leafcn 1 20 40

# Fraction of leaf N in Rubisco (dimensionless)
# Controls efficiency of converting leaf N to photosynthetic capacity
# vcmax25 = flnr × leaf_N × conversion_factor
# Temperate deciduous: 0.08-0.20 (typical for C3 trees)
# Expected impact: ±20-30% GPP change
flnr 1 0.08 0.20

# ============================================================================
# ROOT LONGEVITY PARAMETERS (HIGH SENSITIVITY FROM ORIGINAL ANALYSIS)
# ============================================================================

# Total fine root longevity (years)
# GSA showed: 1.56% GPP change, 1.49% ER change per 10% parameter change
# Controls root turnover rate -> affects ER and N cycling
# Temperate forest: 1-7 years (wider than original 3-10)
froott_long 1 1 7

# Active fine root longevity (years)
# GSA showed: 1.29% GPP change, 1.25% ER change
# Narrower range than AU-Tum (temperate has less variability)
froota_long 1 0.5 3

# Mature fine root longevity (years)
# GSA showed: 2.19% GPP change (highest root parameter sensitivity!)
# This was the most influential root parameter
# Temperate: 0.2-1.5 years (shorter than tropical/mediterranean)
frootm_long 1 0.2 1.5

# ============================================================================
# ROOT C:N PARAMETERS (MODERATE SENSITIVITY, REMOVE REDUNDANCY)
# ============================================================================

# Total fine root C:N ratio (gC/gN)
# GSA showed: 1.34% GPP change, NEE most sensitive (10%)
# Controls root decomposition and N cycling
# Temperate: 30-100 (wider than original 20-184)
froottcn 1 30 100

# NOTE: Removed frootacn and frootmcn due to perfect correlation
# These parameters produced nearly identical model responses
# Model likely only uses total root C:N, not individual pools

# ============================================================================
# ROOT C:P PARAMETERS (REMOVE REDUNDANT, KEEP TOTAL ONLY)
# ============================================================================

# Total fine root C:P ratio (gC/gP)
# Retained but with adjusted range for temperate forest
# Temperate: 400-1000 (narrower than original 375-1125)
froottcp 1 400 1000

# NOTE: Removed frootacp and frootmcp due to perfect correlation
# Sensitivity analysis showed these have <0.3% individual effects
# Not identifiable in calibration

# ============================================================================
# ROOT LITTER QUALITY PARAMETERS (RETAINED TOP PERFORMERS)
# ============================================================================

# Total fine root labile fraction (fraction)
# GSA showed: 0.63% GPP change, 0.89% ER change
# Controls decomposition rate of root litter
frt_flab 1 0.10 0.35

# Total fine root cellulose fraction (fraction)
# GSA showed: minor effect on GPP/ER, but stronger on NEE
frt_fcel 1 0.35 0.65

# Active fine root cellulose fraction
# Moderate effect on NEE (7.4% change)
fra_fcel 1 0.35 0.65

# Mature fine root cellulose fraction
# Similar to above
frm_fcel 1 0.35 0.65

# NOTE: Removed most labile fraction parameters (fra_flab, frm_flab)
# These showed <1% sensitivity

# ============================================================================
# ROOT-LEAF ALLOCATION PARAMETERS
# ============================================================================

# Total fine root to leaf allocation ratio
# Controls biomass partitioning
# Modest effect but helps with C allocation
froott_leaf 1 0.1 0.4

# Active fine root to leaf ratio
froota_leaf 1 0.2 0.6

# ============================================================================
# PARAMETER COUNT: 15 parameters (vs 17 original)
# ============================================================================
# Removed: frootacn, frootmcn, frootacp, frootmcp, fra_flab, frm_flab (6 removed)
# Added: slatop, leafcn, flnr (3 added)
# Net reduction: 3 parameters
#
# Benefits:
# - Eliminates perfect correlations (identifiability fixed)
# - Adds strong GPP controls (photosynthesis parameters)
# - Reduces parameter space dimensionality (faster ensemble)
# - Maintains diversity of parameter types (roots, leaves, allocation)

# ============================================================================
# EXPECTED IMPROVEMENTS
# ============================================================================
# Original ensemble results:
#   GPP: 858 ± 476 gC/m²/year (range: 0-1504)
#   ER:  794 ± 433 gC/m²/year (range: 0-1272)
#   Surrogate GPP range: only 106 gC/m²/year (1143-1249)
#   Surrogate R²: 0.67-0.70 (POOR)
#
# Expected with new parameters:
#   GPP: 1500-3000 gC/m²/year (leaf parameters drive 2-4× increase)
#   ER:  1000-2500 gC/m²/year (coupled to GPP + root parameters)
#   Surrogate GPP range: 500-1000 gC/m²/year (much wider!)
#   Surrogate R²: >0.90 (GOOD) with increased ensemble size
#
# Mechanism:
# - leafcn [20,40]: vcmax25 can vary 2× (40/20)
# - flnr [0.08,0.20]: vcmax25 can vary 2.5× (0.20/0.08)
# - slatop [0.015,0.030]: LAI can vary 2× (0.030/0.015)
# - Combined multiplicative effect: 2 × 2.5 × 2 = 10× GPP range potential
# - Root parameters add another 50-100% variation
# - Total expected range: 5-8× original (matches target!)

# ============================================================================
# ENSEMBLE CONFIGURATION RECOMMENDATIONS
# ============================================================================
# With 15 parameters:
# - Minimum ensemble size: 15 × 100 = 1500 members
# - Recommended: 3000-5000 members (200-330× parameters)
# - Sampling: Sobol sequence (better space-filling than LHS)
#
# In your run script:
#   mycase.nsamples_ensemble = 3000
#   mycase.ensemble_sampling = 'sobol'  # or 'lhs'
#
# Expected compute time (assuming 2 min/member):
#   3000 members × 2 min = 6000 min = 100 hours = 4 days
#   With 50 parallel jobs: 2 hours

# ============================================================================
# VALIDATION TARGETS (US-Blo site)
# ============================================================================
# Observed ranges from FLUXNET data (1997-2007):
# - GPP: ~1500-2500 gC/m²/year (typical temperate deciduous)
# - ER:  ~1000-2000 gC/m²/year
# - NEE: ~-500 to +200 gC/m²/year (interannual variation)
#
# After retraining surrogates, verify:
# - Ensemble GPP covers 1500-2500 range
# - Surrogate R² > 0.90 for GPP, ER
# - No parameter pairs with r > 0.95
# - Run: python diagnose_USBlo_surrogate.py

# ============================================================================
# NOTES ON TEMPERATE VS TROPICAL DIFFERENCES
# ============================================================================
# US-Blo (temperate) vs AU-Tum (mediterranean eucalyptus):
# - Higher SLA: 0.015-0.030 vs 0.005-0.020 (thinner leaves)
# - Lower leaf C:N: 20-40 vs 20-50 (more nitrogen)
# - Shorter root longevity: 1-7 vs 3-10 years (faster cycling)
# - Lower flnr: 0.08-0.20 vs 0.05-0.40 (less variation)
#
# These ranges are based on:
# - Kattge et al. (2011) TRY database
# - Reich & Oleksyn (2004) leaf traits
# - Gill & Jackson (2000) root longevity
